# Campus Customs — environment variables
#
# There is nothing secret to configure here. Every AI model call in this
# project goes through the Claude Code CLI (`claude -p`), authenticated with
# your own Claude Code subscription -- never an API key. In fact, if
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY is set in your environment, the backend explicitly
# scrubs it from the child process before calling `claude` (see
# backend/llm/claude_client.py), so setting one here would do nothing except
# get stripped.
#
# This file exists to satisfy the standard "commit .env.example, gitignore
# the real .env" pattern, and as a place to add real configuration if this
# project ever needs any (e.g. a different backend port). Right now:
#
# Nothing to fill in. Just make sure `claude` is installed and logged in
# (run `claude` once in a terminal and follow the login prompt) before
# starting the backend -- see README.md.
